      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The hospital has often been a place where converging bureaucracy, badly constructed buildings and medical disattention constituted a fertile ground for a growingly inattentive and dehumanising medicine. In Italy the D. M. 20/9/2000 points the attention on the managing of pain in the hospital. It is a radical renewal of the attitude towards pain, involving professional categories working in the hospital, patients and healthy population."},
